---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Bat-Wing FSI Simulation" description="Computational fluid-structure interaction simulation of bat flight with membrane perforations." currentPage="/projects">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Flagship Research Project</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Computational FSI Simulation of Bat Flight</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Investigating how membrane perforations affect aerodynamic performance through
        fluid-structure interaction modeling at the University of Tennessee Space Institute.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Hero visual -->
  <section style="padding:0 0 2rem;">
    <div class="container--wide">
      <div class="placeholder placeholder--hero fade-in">
        <!-- Replace with: hero simulation video or key result visualization -->
        <div>
          <strong>Hero Visual — Bat-Wing Flow Field</strong><br />
          Replace with simulation video (MP4/WebM) or high-res flow visualization<br />
          <em>Recommended: 1200×500, looping video with controls</em>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- Quick summary for recruiters -->
      <div class="card fade-in" style="border-left:4px solid var(--accent); margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-size:1rem; color:var(--steel-blue);">At a Glance</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
          <strong>Role:</strong> Research Intern · Extended and validated an existing FSI codebase
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
          <strong>Advisor:</strong> Dr. Esteban Cisneros-Garibay, UTSI
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
          <strong>Duration:</strong> June 2026 – present
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
          <strong>Stack:</strong> Firedrake, PETSc, Python, Gmsh, VisIt, Slurm/HPC, Git
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Problem statement -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Problem Statement</h2>
        <p>
          Bat wings are thin, flexible membranes that frequently sustain tears and perforations
          from encounters with vegetation, predators, or disease (such as white-nose syndrome).
          Despite these injuries, bats often continue flying — suggesting their flight mechanics
          are somewhat tolerant to membrane damage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Understanding exactly how perforations affect lift, drag, and energy expenditure
          requires high-fidelity computational models that couple the fluid flow with the
          structural response of the membrane — a fluid-structure interaction (FSI) problem.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Methodology -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          The simulation framework uses the finite element method via
          <strong>Firedrake</strong> (built on <strong>PETSc</strong>) for spatial
          discretization. The approach evolved through several stages:
        </p>

        <h3>2D Model → 3D Extension</h3>
        <p>
          Initial work used a 2D flow field coupled with a 1D elastic filament to understand
          the basic coupling mechanics. This was then extended to 3D flapping bat-wing
          geometries with membrane perforations — a significant step up in computational
          complexity.
        </p>

        <h3>Mesh Generation</h3>
        <p>
          Wing geometries are meshed in <strong>Gmsh</strong>. To create anatomically
          accurate models, I extracted wing-boundary coordinates directly from a bat photograph
          and used them to construct the computational mesh.
        </p>

        <!-- Mesh visual -->
        <div class="placeholder fade-in" style="margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <!-- Replace with: mesh visualization image -->
          <span>Mesh visualization — wing geometry with perforation regions (800×400)</span>
        </div>

        <h3>Numerical Methods</h3>
        <p>
          The linear systems are solved using Krylov subspace methods (GMRES) with
          preconditioning, including algebraic multigrid where appropriate. Key numerical
          fixes I implemented:
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Fixed a one-sided traction integral to a two-sided formulation for correct force coupling across the membrane</li>
          <li>Added a Gaussian envelope function to suppress non-physical oscillations at wing tips</li>
          <li>Debugged mesh inversion issues that arose during large membrane deformations</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Validation</h3>
        <p>
          The solver was validated against the <strong>Blasius flat-plate solution</strong> —
          an analytical benchmark for boundary layer flow over a flat surface. This confirmed
          that the velocity profiles and skin friction coefficients matched theory to within
          acceptable tolerances.
        </p>

        <!-- Validation plot -->
        <div class="placeholder fade-in" style="margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <!-- Replace with: Blasius validation comparison plot -->
          <span>Validation plot — computed vs. Blasius analytical solution (800×400)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Energy model -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Energy-Expenditure Model</h2>
        <p>
          Beyond the fluid-structure coupling, I integrated an energy-expenditure model
          that accounts for flow temperature, thermal balance, and mechanical power output.
          This allows parametric studies connecting perforation geometry to the total
          energetic cost of flight.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Current & future -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Current &amp; Future Work</h2>
        <ul style="padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Two-way FSI coupling:</strong> Full bidirectional feedback between fluid forces and membrane deformation</li>
          <li><strong>Leaky-filament conditions:</strong> Modeling flow through perforations with varying sizes and locations</li>
          <li><strong>Parametric studies:</strong> Systematic investigation of how perforation geometry maps to aerodynamic degradation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Media gallery -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h2>Simulation Gallery</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom:1rem;">
          Simulation snapshots, flow visualizations, and result comparisons.
        </p>
        <div class="project-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));">
          <div class="placeholder" style="min-height:180px;">
            <!-- Replace with: simulation video or image -->
            <span>Flow field visualization<br />(video or image)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder" style="min-height:180px;">
            <!-- Replace with: mesh close-up -->
            <span>Mesh detail around perforation<br />(image)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder" style="min-height:180px;">
            <!-- Replace with: pressure contour or comparison plot -->
            <span>Pressure contour / results<br />(image or video)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tech tags -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h2>Tools &amp; Technologies</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.5rem; margin-top:0.75rem;">
          <span class="card__tag">Firedrake</span>
          <span class="card__tag">PETSc</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Python</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Finite Element Method</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Gmsh</span>
          <span class="card__tag">VisIt</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Slurm</span>
          <span class="card__tag">HPC</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Git / GitHub</span>
          <span class="card__tag">GMRES / Krylov</span>
          <span class="card__tag">LaTeX / Beamer</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Back link -->
      <div style="margin-top:3rem;">
        <a href="/projects" class="btn btn--outline">← All Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
